Subject: [PATCH] hifb: allow WQHD OSD on u5pvr

The u5pvr kernel builds HiFB from source. Allow a 2560-pixel HD layer
so the existing height limit also accepts a 2560x1440 EGL framebuffer.
Keep the existing height limit and the other layer capabilities.

Raise HD0 VRAM from 40500 KiB (set by accelmem.patch) to 43200 KiB,
which fits three 2560x1440 buffers at 32 bits per pixel.

This patch is applied after accelmem.patch and only for u5pvr with e2egl.
The HiFB header uses CRLF; preserve its line endings in the patch hunks.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor kernel, u5pvr-specific configuration]

diff --git a/base.mak b/base.mak
--- a/base.mak
+++ b/base.mak
@@ -114,7 +114,7 @@
 # CFG_HI_GFX_DEBUG_LOG_SUPPORT is not set
 CFG_HI_TDE_CSCTMPBUFFER_SIZE=0x0
 CFG_HI_JPEG6B_STREAMBUFFER_SIZE=0x100000
-CFG_HI_HD0_FB_VRAM_SIZE=40500
+CFG_HI_HD0_FB_VRAM_SIZE=43200
 CFG_HI_HD1_FB_VRAM_SIZE=0
 CFG_HI_HD2_FB_VRAM_SIZE=0
 CFG_HI_SD0_FB_VRAM_SIZE=0
diff --git a/drivers/msp/drv/hifb/inc/drv_hifb_config.h b/drivers/msp/drv/hifb/inc/drv_hifb_config.h
--- a/drivers/msp/drv/hifb/inc/drv_hifb_config.h
+++ b/drivers/msp/drv/hifb/inc/drv_hifb_config.h
@@ -405,7 +405,7 @@
     #define CONFIG_HIFB_CURSOR_LAYER_MAXHEIGHT    1080
 #elif defined(CHIP_TYPE_hi3798cv200)   || defined(CHIP_TYPE_hi3798mv200) \
    || defined(CHIP_TYPE_hi3798mv200_a) || defined(CHIP_TYPE_hi3796mv200)
-    #define CONFIG_HIFB_HD_LAYER_MAXWIDTH         1920
+    #define CONFIG_HIFB_HD_LAYER_MAXWIDTH         2560
     #define CONFIG_HIFB_HD_LAYER_MAXHEIGHT        1920/** support vr fmt defined by customer self **/
     #define CONFIG_HIFB_SD_LAYER_MAXWIDTH         720
     #define CONFIG_HIFB_SD_LAYER_MAXHEIGHT        576
